2026-09-27 — conservative code-generation option admission (B08b1)

RED: the driver rejects -fomit-frame-pointer and the three application-projector
tests drop the ten options now covered. This is a driver/projection gap, not a
new optimizer or an assertion that arbitrary GCC tuning flags are ignorable.

Contract: EvoMIR Section 6 still requires every current function's frame.
Omission permission cannot remove a required frame. No sibling-call transform,
optional branch/function padding, automatic loop-array prefetch, loop-header
copying or loop-pattern distribution/libcall pass exists. Their disabling flags
select existing behavior. Mandatory instruction/source/minimum alignment,
explicit source builtins/calls and object-copy lowering remain unchanged.
Positive transform requests and unrelated allocator/reordering flags reject.
The shared application projector preserves the admitted flags in written order.
The ongoing kernel run and its command projector were not changed.

GREEN: focused driver coverage exercises each flag, combined/reversed order at
O0/O2, both interpreters, identical EvoIR/assembly, four retained frame records,
source 64-byte and requested minimum 32-byte alignment, and unsupported positive
flags. The affected gate passes 1,062 tests, zero failures, four existing ignores,
plus Clippy/fmt (against e23c2bd; evocc, evocc-mir, evocc-policy, evocc-proofcheck,
evocc-randgate). All 298 ladder Python tests and targeted Ruff/diff checks pass.

Sealed AArch64 native: 12 executions pass. GCC/Clang baseline O0/O2 supply four
controls; GCC and EvoCC each pass flags and flags+minimum-alignment at O0/O2.
No claim that Clang accepts GCC-only tuning flags is made.

Ten unchanged original musl commands emit and assemble with all ten applicable
options retained: __math_oflow, __math_uflow, frexp, scalbn, AArch64 ceil/floor/
rint/rintf, memcmp and memmove. Outputs match the controls removing only these
newly admitted flags; installed objects remain untouched with unchanged hashes.
The 1,339-record read-only inventory has no omitted newly admitted option.
Remaining GCC allocator/reordering tuning, diagnostic policy and transport/output
actions are separately reported. This does not close B08b or full musl testing.

The retained intermediate driver-final.log contains a test-assertion failure:
the expected assembly omitted the .type directive between .p2align and the
function label. Correcting that assertion yields the final green gate; the
earlier failed/provisional logs are not claimed as passes.

